    <rich_text scale="h1">TEAM &amp; OVERVIEW</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Team SchemaX | Student Information System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Version:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 1.0
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Platform:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> C# Windows Forms (.NET 10)
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> MySQL 8.0
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Development Tool:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Visual Studio 2026
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Repository:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text link="webs https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS">https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Branch:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> develop
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Submission Date:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> October 23, 2026

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">1. Project Overview</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
SchemaX Student Information System (SIS) is a desktop application developed to manage student information and academic records through a MySQL-connected interface.
The system includes user registration and login, dashboard statistics, student record management, searching and filtering, CSV export, student profiles, subject enrollment, grade management, and GWA calculation.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">2. Team Members &amp; Responsibilities</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Zedric Zuñiga</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — UI Layout and DataGridView Display
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Reynalyn Samar</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — MySQL Database Setup and Connection
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Mariane Nuarin</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — CRUD Logic (Add, Edit, Delete)
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Princess Ida Camasis</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Error Handling, Testing, and CherryTree Documentation

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3. Development &amp; Collaboration</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The team used Git and GitHub for collaborative development, with </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">develop</rich_text>
    <rich_text> serving as the integrated project branch.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Tools Used:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Visual Studio 2026, C#, .NET 10, MySQL 8.0, GitHub, CherryTree, and xUnit.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">4. Team Member Contributions</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Zedric Zuñiga — UI Development</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Developed application layouts, navigation, and DataGridView presentation.

• Supported the login, registration, dashboard, and student management interfaces.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Reynalyn Samar — Database Development</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Prepared the MySQL database structure and connection.

◇ Supported database integration, student record retrieval, and dashboard data.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Mariane Nuarin — CRUD Development</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Implemented student Add, View, Edit, and Delete operations.

◇ Integrated student management functions with the database.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Princess Ida Camasis — Error Handling &amp; Documentation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Developed input validation, exception handling, and error logging utilities.

◇ Prepared automated tests, functional test cases, and bug reports.

◇ Organized and maintained the CherryTree documentation.



</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">5. System Features</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">User Management</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ User registration and login

◇ User authentication and account-related functions


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Student Management</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Add, view, edit, and delete student records

◇ Search and filter student information

◇ Student profiles and photo support

◇ CSV data export


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Academic Management</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Subject enrollment and academic records

◇ Grade management and GWA calculation


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">System Support</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Dashboard statistics

◇ MySQL database integration

◇ Input validation and error logging



</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">6. Database Overview</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The system uses the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text> MySQL database with five main tables:
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">users</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Registered user accounts

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">students</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Student information and account ownership

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Subject information

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">student_subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Student enrollment and grades

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">attendance</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Student attendance records


The database structure is provided in </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/schemax_sis.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">7. Testing &amp; Verification</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Automated Validator Testing:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 25/25 PASS — October 16, 2026
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Functional Testing:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 14/14 PASS — October 17, 2026
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Integration Verification:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Successful application build, startup, registration, login, MySQL connectivity, dashboard loading, and student record retrieval — October 22, 2026.
The results represent the recorded testing sessions. Additional academic and GWA tests are included in the project source code.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">8. Final Project Conclusion</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Team SchemaX developed the Student Information System using C# Windows Forms, .NET 10, and MySQL 8.0.
The completed project integrates user authentication, student record management, academic information, database connectivity, input validation, and error handling.
The team demonstrated collaborative development through GitHub and documented the implementation, system setup, functionality, testing results, and technical findings using CherryTree.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Project Version:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 1.0
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Documentation Status:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> COMPLETED FOR SUBMISSION
</rich_text>
