  <node unique_id="2" master_id="0" name="Database Info" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1791553218" ts_lastsave="1792720734">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">DATABASE INFORMATION</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Team SchemaX | Student Information System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">DBMS:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> MySQL
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Assigned Developer:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Reynalyn Samar
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Last Verified:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> October 22, 2026

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">1. Database Overview</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
SchemaX SIS uses MySQL to store student records, user accounts, subjects, grades, and attendance information.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">2. Database Tables</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">students</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Student profiles, academic details, and account ownership (</rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">user_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text>).

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Subject codes, titles, and units.

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">student_subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Student enrollments and grades.

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">attendance</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Student attendance records.

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">users</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Registered accounts, usernames, emails, and password hashes.


The database uses primary keys, unique constraints, and foreign keys to maintain data integrity.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3. Database Connection</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Server:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> localhost

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Port:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 3306

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> schemax_sis

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Configuration:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">appsettings.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text>


The application connects through </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">Db.Open()</rich_text>
    <rich_text>. Database credentials must remain private and must not be uploaded to GitHub.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">4. Database Operations</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">StudentRepository</rich_text>
    <rich_text> class supports:
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Create</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Add student records.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Read</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Retrieve student information.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Update</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Modify existing records.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Delete</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Remove records after confirmation.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Search and Filter</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — Find students by ID, name, year level, or program.


The </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">UserRepository</rich_text>
    <rich_text> handles account registration and authentication, while </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">DashboardRepository</rich_text>
    <rich_text> retrieves student statistics.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">5. Testing and Verification</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">October 17, 2026:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Student CRUD Operations — PASS

◇ Search and Filtering — PASS


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">October 22, 2026:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ MySQL Connection — PASS

◇ User Registration and Login — PASS

◇ Dashboard Loading — PASS

◇ Student Record Retrieval — PASS

◇ Database Backup — PASS
</rich_text>
  </node>
  <node unique_id="3" master_id="0" name="Setup Guide" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1791553256" ts_lastsave="1792720595">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">SETUP GUIDE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Team SchemaX | Student Information System</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">1. Software Requirements</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Windows 11

• Visual Studio 2026 with .NET Desktop Development

• .NET 10 SDK

• MySQL Server and MySQL Workbench

• Git and GitHub



</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">2. Project Installation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Open Visual Studio 2026 and select </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Clone a repository</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

2. Enter: </rich_text>
    <rich_text link="webs https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS.git">https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS.git</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

3. Open the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX.SIS</rich_text>
    <rich_text> solution from the approved branch.

4. Restore dependencies and build using </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Ctrl + Shift + B</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3. Database Setup</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Start MySQL Server and open MySQL Workbench.

2. Create the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text> database using the approved SQL script in </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/schemax_sis.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

3. Verify the required tables: </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">students</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">student_subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">attendance</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, and </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">users</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.

4. Ensure the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">students</rich_text>
    <rich_text> table includes the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">user_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> column.

5. Create </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX.SIS/appsettings.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text> using </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">appsettings.example.json</rich_text>
    <rich_text> and configure the local MySQL connection.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Important:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Back up existing data before executing SQL scripts. Never upload database passwords to GitHub.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">4. Run the Application</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Open the solution in Visual Studio.

2. Build the project.

3. Press </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">F5</rich_text>
    <rich_text> to launch the application.

4. Verify login, dashboard, and student management features.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">5. Troubleshooting</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Build errors:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Check the .NET SDK and restore NuGet packages.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database errors:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Check the MySQL service, connection settings, and required tables.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Login errors:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Verify the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">users</rich_text>
    <rich_text> table.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Dashboard errors:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Verify the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">students.user_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> column.

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">CRUD errors:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Check input validation, student selection, and database connection.</rich_text>
  </node>
  <node unique_id="4" master_id="0" name="App Walkthrough" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1791553353" ts_lastsave="1792720944">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">APP WALKTHROUGH</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
SchemaX Student Information System (SIS) is a C# Windows Forms application connected to a MySQL database. It allows users to manage student information and academic records.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">1. Loading Screen</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Displays the SchemaX SIS logo and loading progress when the application starts.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">2. Login Screen</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Allows registered users to log in using their username and password.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">3. Sign-Up Screen</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Allows new users to register using their personal information and Bicol University email address.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">4. Dashboard</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Displays student statistics, subjects, enrollments, and student distributions by year level and program.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">5. User Profile</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Displays the user's account information and logout option.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">6. Manage Students</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Allows users to add, search, filter, edit, delete, and export student records.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h3">7. Student Record</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
Displays student profiles, subjects, grades, and GWA. Also supports subject management and profile photo uploads.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
